Only these route-local modules plus report-level claims explicitly marked canonical in `docs/state/theorem-state.yaml` are canonical Target C theorem sources at audit.54. Sections 110--121 are canonical report-level entries and are linked below. The exact train-coupled floor endpoint exclusion is also canonical; its detailed proof and independent audit are linked below. The file `95-protected-contact-creation-obstruction-audit.md` remains proof-only and is intentionally outside the canonical reading order.

## Scope rule

The §57 ZR/ZF theorem is on the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`, not the full source:

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3.
\]

Contact-isolated source points remain in the global configuration. Do not extend the affine-kernel conclusion to their coordinates.

## Current route

Audit.54 retains the audit.53 reciprocal/return stack and adds the first canonical **strict full-source replacement criterion** tied to embedded unit-contact walls, together with a collective pentagon-wall extraction theorem.

The baseline full-core structure remains:
\[
\mu_D\ge\mu_{\rm hull}+\varepsilon_*,
\qquad
R_F\ge(\kappa_{\rm fr}-o(1))D,
\qquad
\sigma_C=0,
\]
plus the positive reciprocal \((2,3)\)-sparse train graph, \(|\mathcal O|\ge q-k\), global face-return quotas, and joint bulk/face separator capacity from audit.53.

Canonical \`C-EMBEDDED-WALL-REFILL\` is now the strongest direct source-competitor theorem on the route. If pairwise interior-disjoint actual unit-contact walls \(C_j\) contain old interior populations \(S_j\) and certified wall-safe unit-separated packets of capacities \(M_j\), and if \(T\) is an actual diameter vertex cover, then
\[
\boxed{
\sum_jM_j
\ge
\sum_j|S_j|+|T|
}
\]
produces a same-cardinality unit-separated source of diameter strictly below \(D\).

In the contact-minimal representative, one wall with enough safe sites to replace its interior already gives a contradiction whenever a deleted interior point is contact-nonisolated. Consequences include:

- no actual \(7\times7\) unit square contact patch;
- no \(1/50\)-near-square actual contact perturbation of that patch;
- exclusion of any consecutive oblique affine unit patch satisfying
  \[
  rs(\sin\theta-\sqrt3/2)
  >
  (2-\sqrt3/2)(r+s)-4/\sin\theta.
  \]

Canonical \`C-PENTAGON-WALL-DISJOINT-BULK\` supplies the complementary collective geometry. For any pentagon-to-pentagon train family,
\[
R(\mathcal A)
\ge
c_K\left[R_{PP}-(4+K/2)P\right]_+,
\quad
K=250,
\quad
c_K=\frac1{251^2}\left(\frac{250}{251}\right)^{500},
\]
for a subfamily whose terminal physical pentagon walls are pairwise source-vertex-disjoint.

In the canonical full-core branch
\[
m_B=o(D),\qquad u_B=o(D),\qquad Q-f=o(D),
\]
audit.54 independently derives that the canonical post-hull-depletion quadratic train bulk is asymptotically pentagon-to-pentagon. Therefore one obtains
\[
\boxed{
|\mathcal L|=\Omega(D),\qquad
R(\mathcal L)=\Omega(D^2),\qquad
|x_\tau-y_\tau|=\Omega(D)\ \text{for every }\tau\in\mathcal L,
}
\]
with pairwise source-vertex-disjoint terminal pentagon walls.

Two binding regressions define what the next theorem may **not** assume.

- \`C-FIXED-WALL-ACTIVATION-REGRESSION\`: positive residual, phase mismatch, positive KKT stress, and mixed rigidity do not imply even one fixed-wall spare site; the regular unit pentagon remains locked even after one wall vertex is deleted.
- \`C-LARGE-WALL-LOCK-REGRESSION\`: arbitrarily large near-triangular unit-contact walls with quadratic interior population and positive pinned equilibrium can still admit no strict same-cardinality fixed-wall refill.

The live source-level target is therefore **collective movable-wall activation** or **certified wall surplus sufficient to pay an actual diameter cover**. Universal fixed-wall capacity from residual/phase mismatch is a dead route.

The separate macroscopic-container branch remains open.

